he very soul of the Metro.\n\nThe year is 2039. For a quarter century, the last survivors of nuclear war have been locked in bitter conflict deep in the Metro tunnels beneath the poisoned city of Moscow.\n\nNow, finally, they have been united by a single leader, a fanatical Spartan known as Hunter. But this is no peace: Hunter’s Novoreich regime rules through propaganda and fear, subjugating the population in the name of a new war for the surface against a dark and terrifying enemy.\n\nIn the wilderness beyond the city, the reclusive Stranger is haunted by violent waking nightmares. When the ghosts of his past force him out of exile, he must undertake a harrowing journey into the shattered ruins of Moscow, to the one place he swore he’d never go. The Metro.\n\nExperience the most shocking METRO adventure yet in a powerful single-player story that weaves exploration, survival, combat and stealth across a hauntingly beautiful but deadly world with unparalleled immersion.\n\nInspired by the worldwide best-selling METRO book trilogy by Dmitry Glukhovsky.","summaryPtBr":null,"coverUrl":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/cobxor.jpg","primaryReleaseDate":"2027-02-01T00:00:00Z","firstReleaseDate":"2027-02-01T00:00:00Z","gameType":null,"gameStatus":null,"parentGameId":null,"igdbUrl":"https://www.igdb.com/games/metro-2039","releaseDates":[{"date":"2027-02-01T00:00:00Z","human":"Feb 2027","platformId":6,"platform":"PC","platformName":"PC (Microsoft Windows)","region":"worldwide","status":"Full Release","dateFormatId":1},{"date":"2027-02-01T00:00:00Z","human":"Feb 2027","platformId":167,"platform":"PS5","platformName":"PlayStation 5","region":"worldwide","status":"Full Release","dateFormatId":1},{"date":"2027-02-01T00:00:00Z","human":"Feb 2027","platformId":169,"platform":"Series X|S","platformName":"Xbox Series X|S","region":"worldwide","status":"Full Release","dateFormatId":1}],"bestTrailer":{"id":186941,"name":"Gameplay Trailer","youtubeVideoId":"XLW5LT_RCRk","type":"GAMEPLAY","rank":95},"trailers":[{"id":186941,"name":"Gameplay Trailer","youtubeVideoId":"XLW5LT_RCRk","type":"GAMEPLAY","rank":95},{"id":180994,"name":"Announcement Trailer","youtubeVideoId":"4VBIDuqjQic","type":"ANNOUNCEMENT","rank":88},{"id":181337,"name":"Trailer","youtubeVideoId":"MSdghdelbAw","type":"TRAILER","rank":75},{"id":181338,"name":"Trailer","youtubeVideoId":"doZYgUUIRY4","type":"TRAILER","rank":75}]},{"igdbId":391475,"name":"Shatterswarm","slug":"shatterswarm","summary":"Shatterswarm is a narrative-driven 2D space shooter that combines direct ship combat, fleet command, tower defense, and base building into a strategic colony survival experience. Command Captain Hope's hero ship as you defend Earth's last bastion, The Citadel, against the relentless Voxan Empire.\n\nTake control of your hero ship in intense 2D space combat while simultaneously building and managing a fleet of ships, constructing defensive networks around your citadel, and managing resources to survive wave after wave of alien invaders. Every decision matters as you balance offensive capabilities with defensive structures, all while facing unique enemy types that require different strategies to defeat.\n\nThe game features a diverse roster of challenging enemies, each with distinct mechanics: parasites that hack into and take control of your own ships, motherships that spawn smaller vessels, deflectors that fire your projectiles back at you, and robotic enemies that latch onto your ships and tear them apart. Face off against epic multi-phase boss battles against Voxan commanders Gordox, Gudrak, and the dreaded General Mortex.\n\nWith its perfect blend of action, strategy, and base building, Shatterswarm offers a unique short game experience where tactical thinking and quick reflexes are both essential for survival. The Citadel's survival depends on your strategy—will you focus on overwhelming firepower, impenetrable defenses, or a balanced approach?","summaryPtBr":null,"co